    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2BhZUEU1TftuYrQwcxqutyH)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Based on current `main` (after #517); independent of the other open PRs.\n- #518 (organisation authors) also edits the author-name lint in `sp-academic.org` / `sp-bibprocess.el`, but not these lines (it adds code; this PR adds one function just before `sp-bibtex-merge--section`). A textual conflict is unlikely, and if it happens it is trivial to resolve.\n\n## Cause\n\n- `fab03a4` (dashboard view of the lint reports) turned the merge report into `sp-bibtex-merge--section` and deleted `sp-bibtex-merge--text`.\n- `sp-bibtex-lint-fix-merge` still called `sp-bibtex-merge--text` to build the report it shows before asking, so it died with `Symbol's function definition is void: sp-bibtex-merge--text`.\n- The `** NAME` headings it produces are also what `sp-bibtex-merge--show-group` searches for, so the report is still needed.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Restored `sp-bibtex-merge--text` (as it was before `fab03a4`), in `sp-academic.org` and the tangled `sp-bibprocess.el`.\n- New test `sp-bibtex-merge-test-fix-merge-end-to-end`: runs `sp-bibtex-lint-fix-merge` through the report text, the question, the confirmation and the rewrite. It fails with `void-function sp-bibtex-merge--text` without the fix.\n- Other void functions: byte-compiled `sp-bibprocess.el` with warnings on. `sp-bibtex-merge--text` was the only undefined function from this repo's code (the one other \"not known to be defined\" is `vulpea-buffer-alias-add`, from the vulpea package). I could not compile the other academic modules in the container (it hung on loading dependencies), so they are not checked.\n- `CHANGELOG.org` not edited.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Emacs 29.3 in batch: the 8 `sp-bibtex-merge-test-*` tests pass.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] On a `.bib` with `Hegel, G. W. F.` and `Hegel, Georg Wilhelm Friedrich`: `M-x sp-bibtex-lint-fix-merge` shows the report and the help line, no void-function error\n- [ ] The report scrolls to each group as you step with `n` / `p`\n- [ ] RET on the group, then `yes`: the .bib is rewritten and a backup is made\n- [ ] Step 4 of `M-x sp-bibtex-lint-fix-authors` and the \"merge author names\" entry of the dashboard still start the same command\n- [ ] A `.bib` with no variants: the message \"no variants of one author\" appears\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCLWB5YZ4mKHCo8WZj)_",
